#[section, $md:
    @../../ (Documentation) / @../ (Packages and dependencies) / Core packages

    # Core packages

    Core packages provide typed capabilities owned by the compiler and selected
    by the active builder. They use the same dependency syntax as source packages,
    but binding-backed implementations don't become files in your project.

    Most Core packages require explicit dependency clauses. Unlike large standard-library
    preludes, Moth reserves only a small implicit namespace surface such as `io`.

    Official environments target the complete Core catalogue with documented
    host-capability gates. Custom builders may supply only the implementations
    they need. The reserved `io` namespace alone does not guarantee that a custom
    host implements its operations.

    The @../../progress/packages-and-builders (packages and builders progress
    matrix) records current availability and implementation gaps. @../../lappet
    (Lappet) describes planned native Core support and official package admission.

    ## Package pages

    - @./prelude (Prelude policy)
    - @./io (Core IO)
    - @./collections (Core collections)
    - @./math (Core math)
    - @./text (Core text)
    - @./random (Core random)
    - @./time (Core time)
